All,<br />
<br />
The firm cuts over from Casebridge to Novarra this weekend, February 27-28.=
 Novarra goes live firm-wide Monday at 7:00 a.m. Casebridge becomes read-on=
ly tonight at 8:00 p.m. and will be decommissioned after a verification per=
iod.<br />
<br />
What migrates: all profiled documents on all matters, open and closed, with=
 their profiles, versions and security; matter records; and matter correspo=
ndence filed on or after January 1, 2014.<br />
<br />
What does not migrate: the legacy CommsStore module. Matter correspondence =
filed before January 1, 2014 - roughly 2.1 million messages - is out of sco=
pe for the migration under the project charter approved in October. This ma=
il predates the current filing system, exists in a legacy format the Novarr=
a loader does not accept, and duplicates content retained in the firm's mai=
l journal archive, which remains the firm's retention copy for email under =
the records policy. The archive is unaffected by this weekend's work.<br />
<br />
Practical effect: on older matters, Novarra will show you the documents but=
 not the pre-2014 email trail. For most work this changes nothing. If a mat=
ter genuinely requires the old correspondence, Records can run a journal ar=
chive request.<br />
<br />
Please log any post-cutover issues through the help desk with the prefix NO=
V.<br />
<br />
Anika Chaudhry<br />
Director, Practice Technology<br />
Prescott Vane LLP
